# Qisma — Cursor Project Rules

Expo Router + NativeWind app. **Design language: Nothing OS** — monochrome,
industrial, minimal, technical, restrained, typography-first, tactile,
high whitespace, calm motion.

TypeScript strict, React 19, Expo SDK 54, React Native 0.81.

---

## Design Identity (read first)

The UI must feel like **Nothing OS / premium hardware software / industrial
minimalism / technical futuristic interface**.

It must NOT feel like: generic SaaS dashboard, Material Design app, colorful
startup landing page, gaming UI, or social media app.

When in doubt: **remove**, don't add. Whitespace > separators. Type > chrome.

---

## Visual Rules

- Near-black backgrounds (`bg-background`, `bg-surface*`).
- Semantic surface hierarchy — use `surfaceBase / surfaceElevated / surfaceFloating / surfaceRaised / surfaceOverlay` instead of arbitrary tints.
- **Thin borders, not shadows.** Prefer `border border-border` over elevation.
- Outlined components > filled components.
- Whitespace > separators / dividers.
- Restrained contrast — avoid pure-white-on-pure-black slabs of text.
- Conservative `rounded-*` — small radii (`rounded-sm`/`rounded-md`/`rounded-card`), never pill-everything.

**Forbidden:** colorful UI, gradients (unless explicitly requested),
neumorphism, Material Design styling, glassmorphism-heavy UI, random
elevation shadows, decorative UI without function, oversized CTA buttons.

---

## Color Rules

- **Never hardcode colors.** Always import from `@/theme`.
- Monochrome palette only. The `accent` is reserved for: focus rings, selected state, single primary CTA per screen, key status indicators.
- Use subtle overlays (`overlay`, `overlayStrong`, `glass`) instead of colorful fills.
- Status colors (`success`, `error`, `warning`, `info`) only for genuine status — never decorative.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded hex, won't react to theme
<View style={{ backgroundColor: '#0A0A0A' }} />
<View className="bg-purple-500" />

// ❌ BAD — static `colors` import is dark-only, ignores theme switch
import { colors } from '@/theme';
<View style={{ backgroundColor: colors.surfaceElevated }} />

// ✅ GOOD — subscribes to active palette, flips on theme toggle
import { useThemeColors } from '@/theme';
const palette = useThemeColors();
<View style={{ backgroundColor: palette.surfaceElevated }} />
```

---

## Theme Awareness — EVERYTHING is Light + Dark

Every component, screen, and primitive we ship MUST render correctly in both
light and dark. This is non-negotiable. The active palette is selected by
`<ThemeProvider>` (already mounted at the root) and resolves `system` /
`light` / `dark` preferences.

### Rules

- **Always read colors via `useThemeColors()`** in components. The static
  `colors` export is the dark palette — fine for token-time constants
  (e.g. inside `theme/borders.ts` presets) but wrong inside JSX.
- Both palettes have **identical keys** (`palette.background`,
  `palette.textPrimary`, etc.). No `if (mode === 'dark')` branching.
- For Reanimated `useAnimatedStyle`, pass palette colors as the **second-arg
  deps** so the animated style re-evaluates on theme swap:
  ```tsx
  const palette = useThemeColors();
  const style = useAnimatedStyle(
    () => ({ borderColor: interpolateColor(p.value, [0, 1], [palette.border, palette.borderFocus]) }),
    [palette.border, palette.borderFocus],
  );
  ```
- Layout-only `StyleSheet.create` is fine; layer palette-dependent props as
  inline overrides on the JSX (`style={[styles.x, { color: palette.textPrimary }]}`).
  Inline styles are only forbidden when expressible as tokens — palette
  swap is the explicit exception.
- Status bar / chrome must derive from `useThemeMode()` (`'light' | 'dark'`).
- **Test in both modes** before merging — the auth screen has a `ThemeToggle`
  for instant flipping during development.

### NativeWind colour caveat

`bg-background`, `text-textPrimary`, etc. currently resolve to the **dark**
palette only (Tailwind config consumes the dark tokens). Until we wire
NativeWind's `dark:` variants:

- ❌ Don't use NativeWind utility classes for color-sensitive surfaces.
- ✅ Layout-only NativeWind utilities (`flex-*`, `p-*`, `gap-*`,
  `rounded-*`, `border` width-only) are still encouraged.

### Light-mode accent

In light mode, `palette.accent` is ink-black (`#0A0A0A`), not lime. Don't
write code that assumes a specific accent hue — read the token.

---

## Typography Rules

Typography is the **primary visual element**.

- Use **mono** (`font-mono*` / `textStyles.code*` / `typography.fontFamily.mono`) for: labels, metadata, timestamps, technical info, counters, status text, IDs, version numbers.
- Use **uppercase** for system labels (combine with `textStyles.overline` or `tracking-widest uppercase`).
- Large headings use **restrained weight** — prefer `semiBold` (600) over `bold` (700) for display sizes; reserve `bold` for true emphasis.
- Avoid overly bold typography across the board.
- **Tabular numbers** for clocks, stats, prices, counters (use `textStyles.numeric*`).

```tsx
// metadata
<Text className="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-textMuted">
  v1.0.0 · BUILD 240
</Text>

// heading — restrained weight
<Text style={textStyles.h1}>Account</Text>  // already semiBold/bold per scale

// stat — tabular
<Text style={textStyles.numericLarge}>42</Text>
```

---

## Spacing Rules

- **Strict spacing scale only.** Use `spacing.*` tokens or NativeWind `p-*`/`m-*`/`gap-*` (which map to the same scale).
- Respect 8pt grid — the spacing scale is built on it.
- Spacious & intentional layouts. Generous `gap-*` between sections.
- **Forbidden:** arbitrary spacing (`style={{ padding: 13 }}`, `className="p-[7px]"`), dense UI.

---

## Component Rules

- **Always reuse existing primitives** in `@/components` (Button, Input, Card, Text, Pressable, Avatar, Badge, Divider, Screen, Skeleton).
- Keep components minimal. Composition > nesting.
- No unnecessary decorations, no excessive shadows.
- Outlined Button variants by default; filled only for the single primary action.

---

## Motion Rules

Motion is **mechanical and calm**. Use `@/theme` motion tokens.

- Subtle fade & slide transitions only.
- **No bounce, no playful springs.** Prefer `transition.standard` / `easing.standard`.
- Restrained durations — use `duration.fast` / `duration.standard`; reserve `duration.slow` for full-screen transitions.
- **Forbidden:** cartoon animations, exaggerated spring, parallax for its own sake.
- ⚠️ **Always import `Easing` from `react-native-reanimated`**, never from
  `react-native`. The latter is not a worklet and throws at runtime when used
  with `withTiming` / `withSpring`. (Our `easing.*.rn` tokens already do this.)

```tsx
import { duration, easing } from '@/theme';
withTiming(1, { duration: duration.standard.ms, easing: easing.standard.rn });
```

---

## Folder Structure (sacred — keep it)

```
src/
├── api/                  HTTP client, queryClient, endpoints, base URL resolver
├── app/                  Expo Router routes (config: extra.router.root = 'src/app')
│   ├── (auth)/           Auth route group
│   └── (tabs)/           Main tab group
├── components/ui/        Theme-driven primitives (Button, Input, Card, ...)
├── constants/            Static config, route names, query keys, storage keys
├── features/<name>/      Vertical slice — api/, components/, hooks/, screens/, store/, types/
│   └── auth | home | notifications | profile
├── hooks/                Cross-cutting hooks (useColorScheme, useAppState, ...)
├── i18n/                 i18next setup + locales/
├── navigation/           Navigator types & linking config
├── services/             Side-effect singletons (analytics, storage, notifications)
├── store/                Global zustand stores
├── theme/                ⚠️ SOURCE OF TRUTH — see rules below
├── types/                Ambient & shared types
└── utils/                Pure helpers (cn, formatters, validators, ...)
```

**Don't** add new top-level folders without a strong reason.
**Do** keep `.gitkeep` in empty scaffold dirs.

---

## Theme — Single Source of Truth

`src/theme/*.tokens.ts` is consumed by **both** `tailwind.config.ts` and the
`.ts` façades. NEVER hardcode colors, spacing, radii, font sizes, etc.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<View style={{ padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#0A0A0A', borderRadius: 12 }} />
<Text style={{ fontSize: 24, fontWeight: '700', color: '#FAFAFA' }}>Hi</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — NativeWind utilities for layout (spacing/radius/typography only)
<View className="p-4 rounded-card" />
<Text className="text-2xl font-sans-semibold">Hi</Text>

// ✅ GOOD — palette via the hook (theme-aware)
import { spacing, textStyles, useThemeColors } from '@/theme';
const palette = useThemeColors();
<Text style={[textStyles.h1, { color: palette.textPrimary }]}>Hi</Text>
```

Adding a token? Edit the `.tokens.ts` file → it auto-flows to Tailwind + TS.

Read `src/theme/THEME.md` before touching anything in `src/theme/`.

---

## Imports

- Use `@/` path alias (configured in `tsconfig.json`) — never relative `../../..`.
- Re-export feature publics from `features/<name>/index.ts` when one is added.
- Barrel `@/theme` for tokens; barrel `@/components` for UI primitives.

---

## Code Style

- TypeScript `strict` + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` — handle `undefined` from arrays/records.
- Prefer functional components; no class components.
- **Avoid inline styles** when expressible as NativeWind utilities or theme tokens. Palette-from-`useThemeColors()` overrides on JSX are the explicit exception.
- No comments that narrate what code does (`// increment counter`). Only comments that explain non-obvious *why*, trade-offs, or constraints.
- Run `pnpm format` (Prettier) and `pnpm lint` before committing.

---

## Routing (Expo Router)

- Routes live in `src/app/` (NOT root `app/`).
- Group folders use parens: `(auth)`, `(tabs)`.
- Layouts: `_layout.tsx` per route group.
- Use typed routes (`experiments.typedRoutes: true` in `app.config.ts`).
- Route files stay thin — extract logic into `features/<name>/screens/`.

---

## When Generating UI — Checklist

1. Reuse theme tokens (`@/theme`) — no hex, no px, no arbitrary values.
2. **Theme-aware:** colors come from `useThemeColors()`. Verify the screen looks right in BOTH light and dark before declaring done (use the in-app `ThemeToggle`).
3. Match Nothing-style patterns — monochrome, thin borders, generous whitespace.
4. Lead with typography & spacing; chrome is a last resort.
5. Reuse `@/components/ui` primitives; don't reinvent Button/Input/Card.
6. Reduce visual noise — if a divider, shadow, or color isn't earning its place, delete it.

---

## Don't Reintroduce

- Hardcoded hex / px / rem values in components.
- Static `colors.X` references inside JSX (use `useThemeColors()` — the static export is dark-only and breaks light mode).
- NativeWind colour utilities for theme-sensitive surfaces (`bg-background`, `text-textPrimary`) — they only render dark today.
- Inline `StyleSheet.create` for things expressible as NativeWind layout classes.
- Business logic in `src/app/*` route files — extract to `features/<name>/`.
- New global stores when a feature-local store would do.
- Random elevation shadows, gradients, colorful fills, oversized CTAs, bouncy animations.
- New screens / components that haven't been verified in BOTH light and dark.
